{
  "schema": "quantrule.research-program/v1",
  "program_id": "PROGRAM-2026-11-04-01",
  "premise": "A confirmed RSI divergence at a confirmed major pivot marks exhaustion (regular) or continuation (hidden); after the pivot is confirmed, price reaches +2 ATR in the divergence direction before -1 ATR within 20 15m bars more often than the unconditional base.",
  "economic_rationale": "A divergence at a structural pivot is a failed-momentum signal; the confirmed pivot gives a reference for the stop, and the confirmation delay is part of the claim rather than an approximation.",
